report "Azeroth | Profession Leveling Planner"
  nav "Azeroth Field Guide"
    link "Overview" -> "#overview"
    link "Profession routes" -> "#records"
    link "Leveling notes" -> "#activity"
  heading
    eyebrow: "WOW CLASSIC / ERA · 1–300"
    title: "Every profession, one step at a time."
    subtitle: "Choose a profession tab for its skill brackets, recipe counts, and ingredients. Crafting quantities follow the Wowhead fast or suggested path; gatherers show what to target at each bracket."
    meta: "WOWHEAD CLASSIC GUIDES · MATERIAL COUNTS BY SKILL RANGE · 12 PROFESSION TABS"
  feature
    label: "START HERE"
    title: "Follow the rows from top to bottom"
    text: "The count is the number of crafts or the suggested gather targets for that bracket. Materials show the total needed for that row, including saved intermediates where indicated. Trainers, recipe books, and rare patterns are called out in the relevant steps."
    status: "Step-by-step"
    tooltip: "Yellow and green recipes can require extra attempts. Counts are route estimates rather than guarantees."
  callout
    title: "Reading the numbers"
    text: "Wowhead describes several shopping lists as minimum or approximate. Orange recipes are the reliable skillups; yellow and green recipes can take more crafts. Gathering professions do not have fixed craft counts, so those tabs show skill targets and materials to gather instead. Prices and stock vary by realm."
  metrics
    metric "Profession tabs" | "12" | "Nine primary, three secondary"
    metric "Target skill" | "300" | "Classic Era"
    metric "Count basis" | "Per range" | "Craft total or suggested gather target"
    metric "Trainer stops" | "50 / 125 / 200+" | "Check rank gates in each route"
  professions
    profession "Alchemy" | "Primary · Crafting" | "Fast route from Minor Healing Potion to Major Healing Potion. Keep the Philosopher's Stone for transmutes. Wowhead: https://www.wowhead.com/classic/guide/alchemy-leveling-1-300-wow-classic"
      step "1–60" | "Minor Healing Potion" | "59 crafts" | "59 Peacebloom + 59 Silverleaf + 59 Empty Vials. Save the potions for the next step."
      step "60–110" | "Lesser Healing Potion" | "59 crafts" | "59 Minor Healing Potions + 59 Briarthorn."
      step "110–140" | "Healing Potion" | "30 crafts" | "30 Bruiseweed + 30 Briarthorn + 30 Leaded Vials."
      step "140–155" | "Lesser Mana Potion" | "15 crafts" | "15 Mageroyal + 15 Stranglekelp + 15 Empty Vials. Train Expert before 150."
      step "155–185" | "Greater Healing Potion" | "30 crafts" | "30 Liferoot + 30 Kingsblood + 30 Leaded Vials."
      step "185–215" | "Agility then Greater Defense Elixirs" | "25 + 10 crafts" | "Agility: 25 Stranglekelp + 25 Goldthorn + 25 Leaded Vials. Defense: 10 Wild Steelbloom + 10 Goldthorn + 10 Leaded Vials."
      step "215–230" | "Superior Healing Potion" | "15 crafts" | "15 Sungrass + 15 Khadgar's Whisker + 15 Crystal Vials. Train Artisan before 225."
      step "230–231" | "Philosopher's Stone" | "1 craft" | "4 Iron Bars + 1 Black Vitriol + 4 Purple Lotus + 4 Firebloom. Keep it."
      step "231–265" | "Detect Undead then Greater Agility" | "19 + 15 crafts" | "Detect Undead: 19 Arthas' Tears + 19 Crystal Vials. Greater Agility: 15 Sungrass + 15 Goldthorn + 15 Crystal Vials."
      step "265–300" | "Superior Mana then Major Healing Potion" | "20 + about 18 crafts" | "Superior Mana: 40 Sungrass + 40 Blindweed + 20 Crystal Vials. Major Healing: 36 Golden Sansam + 18 Mountain Silversage + 18 Crystal Vials."
    profession "Blacksmithing" | "Primary · Crafting" | "Turn mined stone into saved grinding stones, then move through Bronze, Iron, Mithril, and Thorium recipes. The 260–300 route assumes access to dropped plans. Wowhead: https://www.wowhead.com/classic/guide/blacksmithing-leveling-1-300-wow-classic"
      step "1–75" | "Rough and Coarse Sharpening / Grinding Stones" | "40 + about 60 + about 25 crafts" | "40 Rough Stone; 120 Rough Stone for saved Rough Grinding Stones; 25 Coarse Stone. Continue with about 35 Coarse Grinding Stones using 70 Coarse Stone."
      step "75–90" | "Coarse Grinding Stones" | "about 35 crafts" | "70 Coarse Stone. Save these for later recipes."
      step "90–125" | "Runed Copper Belts, Silver Rods, Bronze Leggings" | "15 belts + 5 rods + 15 leggings" | "Belts: 150 Copper Bars total. Rods: 5 Silver Bars + 10 Rough Grinding Stones. Leggings: 90 Bronze Bars."
      step "125–140" | "Heavy Grinding Stones" | "about 35 crafts" | "105 Heavy Stone. Save these for later recipes."
      step "125–155" | "Heavy Grinding Stones, Bracers, Golden Rods" | "about 35 + 10 + 5 crafts" | "105 Heavy Stone; 50 Bronze Bars + 20 Coarse Grinding Stones; 5 Gold Bars + 10 Coarse Grinding Stones. Save the grinding stones."
      step "155–200" | "Green Iron and Golden Scale pieces" | "10 + 25 + 10 crafts" | "Leggings: 80 Iron Bars + 10 Heavy Grinding Stones + 10 Green Dye. Bracers: 150 Iron Bars + 25 Green Dye. Golden Scale: 50 Steel Bars + 20 Heavy Grinding Stones."
      step "200–225" | "Solid Grinding Stones then Heavy Mithril Gauntlets" | "about 30 + 15 crafts" | "120 Solid Stone for saved stones. Gauntlets: 90 Mithril Bars + 60 Mageweave Cloth. Train Artisan between 200 and 225; character level 35+."
      step "225–250" | "Steel Plate Helm then Mithril Coif" | "10 + 15 crafts" | "Helms: 140 Steel Bars + 10 Solid Grinding Stones. Coifs: 150 Mithril Bars + 90 Mageweave Cloth. Mithril Spurs are an alternative if you know the plan."
      step "250–260" | "Dense Sharpening Stones" | "about 20 crafts" | "20 Dense Stone."
      step "260–275" | "Thorium Belt then Thorium Bracers" | "10 + 5 crafts" | "Belts: 120 Thorium Bars + 40 Red Power Crystals. Bracers: 60 Thorium Bars + 20 Blue Power Crystals. Plans are tradeable drops."
      step "275–300" | "Imperial Plate Bracers then Thorium Boots" | "15 + 10 crafts" | "Bracers: 300 Thorium Bars + 15 Star Rubies. Boots: 200 Thorium Bars + 80 Rugged Leather + 40 Green Power Crystals. Alternative plans change totals."
    profession "Enchanting" | "Primary · Crafting" | "Make rods you keep, enchant bracers and cloaks, then use dust-heavy enchants and Lesser Mana Oil. Disenchanting suitable gear can offset reagent costs. Wowhead: https://www.wowhead.com/classic/guide/enchanting-leveling-1-300-wow-classic"
      step "1–50" | "Runed Copper Rod then Minor Health" | "1 rod + 48 enchants" | "Rod: 1 Copper Rod + 1 Strange Dust + 1 Lesser Magic Essence. Enchant: 48 Strange Dust."
      step "50–100" | "Minor Health, Minor Stamina, Runed Silver Rod" | "about 60 + 10 + 1" | "Health: about 60 Strange Dust. Stamina: 30 Strange Dust. Rod: 1 Silver Rod + 6 Strange Dust + 3 Greater Magic Essence + 1 Shadowgem. Train Journeyman."
      step "101–135" | "Greater Magic Wands then Minor Agility Cloaks" | "9 + 25 crafts" | "Wands: 9 Simple Wood + 9 Greater Magic Essence. Cloaks: 25 Lesser Astral Essence. Obtain the cloak formula from the faction vendor."
      step "135–185" | "Lesser Stamina and Lesser Strength Bracers" | "20 + about 40 crafts" | "Stamina: 40 Soul Dust. Strength: about 80 Soul Dust. Train Expert before 150."
      step "185–225" | "Strength Bracers and Greater Defense Cloaks" | "15 + about 25 + 5 crafts" | "Strength: about 40 Vision Dust total across both brackets. Cloaks: 15 Vision Dust. Make Runed Golden Rod at 155–156 and Runed Truesilver Rod at 200–201; keep both."
      step "225–250" | "Agility Gloves, Stamina Boots, Superior Health Chest" | "5 + 5 + about 25 crafts" | "Gloves: 5 Lesser Nether Essence + 5 Vision Dust. Boots: 25 Vision Dust. Chest: about 150 Vision Dust. Train Artisan before 225."
      step "250–294" | "Lesser Mana Oil then Greater Stamina Shield" | "about 20 + about 30 crafts" | "Oil: about 60 Dream Dust + 40 Purple Lotus + 20 Crystal Vials. Shield: about 300 Dream Dust. Formulas are vendor gated; oil turns yellow at 260 and shield at 285."
      step "294–295" | "Runed Arcanite Rod" | "1 craft" | "1 Arcanite Rod + 1 Golden Pearl + 10 Illusion Dust + 4 Greater Eternal Essence + 4 Small Brilliant Shards + 2 Large Brilliant Shards. Keep it."
      step "295–300" | "Superior Defense Cloak" | "5 crafts" | "40 Illusion Dust."
    profession "Engineering" | "Primary · Crafting" | "Make and keep intermediate powders, bolts, tubes, frameworks, triggers, and casings; use bombs and gadgets for the skill brackets. Wowhead: https://www.wowhead.com/classic/guide/engineering-leveling-1-300-wow-classic"
      step "1–75" | "Rough Powder, Copper Bolts, Arclight Spanner, Copper Bombs" | "60 + 30 + 1 + about 30 crafts" | "60 Rough Stone; 36 Copper Bars for bolts and spanner; bombs also use 30 Copper Bars, 60 Rough Blasting Powder, 30 Bolts, and 30 Linen Cloth."
      step "75–105" | "Coarse Powder, Dynamite, Silver Contacts" | "about 60 + about 20 + 5 crafts" | "60 Coarse Stone; dynamite uses 60 Coarse Blasting Powder + 20 Linen Cloth; contacts use 5 Silver Bars."
      step "105–135" | "Bronze Tubes and Standard Scopes" | "25 tubes + 10 scopes" | "Tubes: 50 Bronze Bars + 25 Weak Flux. Scopes: 10 Bronze Tubes + 10 Moss Agates. Save the tubes."
      step "135–175" | "Heavy Powder, Bronze Gizmos, Frameworks, Explosive Sheep" | "30 + 15 + 15 + 15 crafts" | "30 Heavy Stone; Gizmos: 30 Bronze Bars + 15 Wool Cloth; Frameworks: 30 Bronze Bars + 15 Medium Leather + 15 Wool Cloth; Sheep use saved parts, powder, and 30 Wool Cloth."
      step "175–200" | "Micro-Adjustor, Solid Powder, Mithril Tubes" | "1 + 60 + about 7 crafts" | "Adjustor: 4 Steel Bars. Powder: 120 Solid Stone. Tubes: 21 Mithril Bars. Train Artisan between 200 and 225."
      step "200–238" | "Unstable Triggers then Mithril Casings" | "20 + 40 crafts" | "Triggers: 20 Mithril Bars + 20 Mageweave Cloth + 20 Solid Blasting Powder. Casings: 120 Mithril Bars. Save both."
      step "238–260" | "Hi-Explosive Bombs then Dense Powder" | "20 + about 30 crafts" | "Bombs use 40 Mithril Casings + 20 Unstable Triggers + 40 Solid Blasting Powder. Dense Powder: 60 Dense Stone. Save powder."
      step "260–285" | "Thorium Widgets" | "about 35 crafts" | "105 Thorium Bars + 35 Runecloth. Buy Schematic: Thorium Widget from the faction city vendor."
      step "285–300" | "Thorium Shells" | "15 crafts" | "30 Thorium Bars + 15 saved Dense Blasting Powder. Requires the world-drop schematic; Thorium Tubes are the fallback."
    profession "Herbalism" | "Primary · Gathering" | "Gather while questing, using Find Herbs. Targets below are the guide's herb skill thresholds, not a required number of herbs to collect. Wowhead: https://www.wowhead.com/classic/guide/herbalism-leveling-1-300-wow-classic"
      step "1–70" | "Peacebloom, Silverleaf, Earthroot, Mageroyal" | "Skill target 70" | "Gather early herbs in your starting zones; train Journeyman at 50–75."
      step "70–115" | "Mageroyal, Briarthorn, Stranglekelp, Bruiseweed" | "Skill target 115" | "Gather any eligible node; Stranglekelp is coastal."
      step "115–170" | "Wild Steelbloom through Fadeleaf" | "Skill target 170" | "Add Grave Moss, Kingsblood, Liferoot, and Fadeleaf; train Expert at 125–150."
      step "170–230" | "Goldthorn, Khadgar's Whisker, Wintersbite, Firebloom, Purple Lotus" | "Skill target 230" | "Train Artisan at 200–225. Follow faction and zone availability."
      step "230–270" | "Sungrass, Blindweed, Ghost Mushroom, Gromsblood, Golden Sansam" | "Skill target 270" | "Use the herb list matching your current skill; focus on eligible dense routes."
      step "270–300" | "Dreamfoil, Mountain Silversage, Plaguebloom, Icecap" | "Skill target 300" | "Continue gathering eligible high-level herbs; route maps depend on your faction and competition."
    profession "Leatherworking" | "Primary · Crafting" | "Use scraps and leather kits early, save cured hides and grinding materials for later recipes, then finish with Wicked Leather patterns. Wowhead: https://www.wowhead.com/classic/guide/leatherworking-leveling-1-300-wow-classic"
      step "1–55" | "Light Leather, Light Armor Kits, Cured Light Hides" | "30 + about 18 + 10 crafts" | "90 Ruined Leather Scraps; 18 Light Leather; 10 Light Hides + 10 Salt."
      step "55–100" | "Embossed Gloves then Fine Leather Belts" | "30 + 15 crafts" | "Gloves: 90 Light Leather + 60 Coarse Thread. Belts: 90 Light Leather + 30 Coarse Thread."
      step "100–150" | "Cured Medium Hides, Dark Leather Boots and Belts" | "15 + 22 + 15 crafts" | "Cured Medium: 15 Medium Hides + 15 Salt. Boots: 88 Medium Leather + 44 Fine Thread + 22 Gray Dye. Belts use 15 saved Fine Leather Belts, 15 Cured Medium Hides, thread, and dye."
      step "150–180" | "Heavy Armor Kits" | "about 22 crafts" | "110 Heavy Leather + 22 Fine Thread."
      step "180–200" | "Barbaric Shoulders then Guardian Gloves" | "10 + 10 crafts" | "Shoulders: 80 Heavy Leather + 10 Cured Heavy Hides + 20 Fine Thread. Gloves: 40 Heavy Leather + 10 Cured Heavy Hides + 10 Silken Thread."
      step "200–220" | "Thick Armor Kits" | "20 crafts" | "100 Thick Leather + 20 Silken Thread. Train Artisan before 225."
      step "220–250" | "Nightscape Headbands then Pants" | "about 11 + 20 crafts" | "Headbands: 55 Thick Leather + 22 Silken Thread. Pants: 280 Thick Leather + 80 Silken Thread. Save 2 headbands and 2 pants if choosing Tribal specialization."
      step "250–290" | "Rugged Armor Kits then Wicked Leather Gauntlets" | "about 12 + about 32 crafts" | "Kits: 60 Rugged Leather. Gauntlets: 256 Rugged Leather + 32 Black Dye + 32 Rune Thread."
      step "290–300" | "Wicked Leather Headbands" | "10 crafts" | "120 Rugged Leather + 10 Black Dye + 10 Rune Thread. Pattern is a tradeable drop; alternatives need other patterns."
    profession "Mining" | "Primary · Gathering" | "Mine eligible veins while questing or running zone loops. Smelting can bridge early skill gaps, but the guide says it stops being effective after 185. Wowhead: https://www.wowhead.com/classic/guide/mining-leveling-1-300-wow-classic"
      step "1–65" | "Copper Veins" | "Skill target 65" | "Carry a Mining Pick and turn on Find Minerals. Train Journeyman at 50–75."
      step "65–125" | "Tin and Silver Veins" | "Skill target 125" | "Smelting Silver can help with the Tin-to-Mithril gap if ore is available. Train Expert at 125–150."
      step "125–175" | "Iron and Gold Veins" | "Skill target 175" | "Follow eligible node spawns in the route zones."
      step "175–245" | "Mithril and Truesilver Deposits" | "Skill target 245" | "Train Artisan at 200–225. Smelting is no longer an effective leveling method after 185."
      step "245–300" | "Small and Rich Thorium Veins" | "Skill target 300" | "Use the guide's high-level zone routes; node skill requirements gate access."
    profession "Skinning" | "Primary · Gathering" | "Skin every eligible beast while questing or grinding. There is no fixed itinerary: move from low-level to higher-level mobs as your skill rises. Wowhead: https://www.wowhead.com/classic/guide/skinning-leveling-1-300-wow-classic"
      step "1–50" | "Skin low-level beasts" | "Skill target 50" | "Match mob level to your skinning cap; gather Ruined Leather Scraps and Light Leather."
      step "50–125" | "Move through progressively higher mobs" | "Skill target 125" | "Target mobs that yield Light and Medium Leather; train Journeyman and Expert at their skill gates."
      step "125–200" | "Continue into mid-level beast zones" | "Skill target 200" | "Gather Medium and Heavy Leather; train the next rank at 200."
      step "200–300" | "Skin high-level beasts as you quest" | "Skill target 300" | "Progress into Thick and Rugged Leather mob bands; use Wowhead's skinning route map for dense farming areas."
    profession "Tailoring" | "Primary · Crafting" | "This is Wowhead's fast method. Turn cloth into bolts in batches, then use the listed garments. Budget Bolts & Bags is a separate cheaper option. Wowhead: https://www.wowhead.com/classic/guide/tailoring-leveling-1-300-wow-classic"
      step "1–75" | "Linen Bolts, Linen Belts, Reinforced Capes" | "95 bolts + 25 belts + 5 capes" | "190 Linen Cloth. Belts use 25 Coarse Thread; capes use 10 Linen Bolts + 15 Coarse Thread."
      step "75–125" | "Wool Bolts, Simple Kilts, Double-stitched Shoulders" | "45 bolts + 15 kilts + 15 shoulders" | "135 Wool Cloth. Kilts: 60 Linen Bolts + 15 Fine Thread. Shoulders: 45 Wool Bolts + 30 Fine Thread."
      step "125–160" | "Silk Bolts and Azure Silk Hoods" | "205 bolts + 20 hoods" | "820 Silk Cloth. Hoods use 40 Silk Bolts + 20 Fine Thread + 40 Blue Dye. Train Expert before 150."
      step "160–175" | "Silk Headbands and Formal White Shirts" | "10 + 5 crafts" | "Headbands: 30 Silk Bolts + 20 Fine Thread. Shirts: 15 Silk Bolts + 5 Fine Thread + 10 Bleach."
      step "175–185" | "Mageweave Bolts" | "100 bolts" | "500 Mageweave Cloth."
      step "185–220" | "Crimson Silk clothing, Orange Mageweave Shirt" | "20 vests + 10 pants + 5 shirts" | "Vests: 80 Silk Bolts + 40 Fine Thread + 40 Red Dye. Pants: 40 Silk Bolts + 20 Silken Thread + 20 Red Dye. Shirts: 5 Mageweave Bolts + 5 Heavy Silken Thread + 5 Orange Dye. Train Artisan before 225."
      step "220–250" | "Black Mageweave Gloves and Headbands" | "10 + 25 crafts" | "Gloves: 20 Mageweave Bolts + 20 Heavy Silken Thread. Headbands: 75 Mageweave Bolts + 50 Heavy Silken Thread."
      step "250–280" | "Runecloth Bolts then Runecloth Belts" | "155 bolts + 25 belts" | "775 Runecloth. Belts use 75 Runecloth Bolts + 25 Rune Thread."
      step "280–300" | "Runecloth Gloves" | "20 crafts" | "80 Runecloth Bolts + 80 Rugged Leather + 20 Rune Thread. Buy the limited-supply pattern from Qia in Winterspring."
    profession "Cooking" | "Secondary · Crafting" | "Wowhead calls the all-fish route the easiest and cheapest. Cook in the city while leveling Fishing; obtain the Expert and Artisan books/quest when required. Wowhead: https://www.wowhead.com/classic/guide/cooking-leveling-1-300-wow-classic"
      step "1–50" | "Brilliant Smallfish" | "50 crafts" | "50 Raw Brilliant Smallfish."
      step "50–100" | "Longjaw Mud Snapper" | "50 crafts" | "50 Raw Longjaw Mud Snapper. Train Journeyman before 75."
      step "100–150" | "Bristle Whisker Catfish" | "50 crafts" | "50 Raw Bristle Whisker Catfish. Learn Expert before 150."
      step "150–175" | "Bristle Whisker Catfish" | "70 crafts" | "70 Raw Bristle Whisker Catfish."
      step "175–225" | "Mithril Head Trout" | "60 crafts" | "60 Raw Mithril Head Trout. Learn Artisan before 225; requires character level 35+ and a quest."
      step "225–275" | "Spotted Yellowtail" | "70 crafts" | "70 Raw Spotted Yellowtail."
      step "275–300" | "Mightfish Steak" | "25 crafts" | "25 Large Raw Mightfish + 25 Hot Spices + 25 Soothing Spices. Lobster Stew or Baked Salmon are alternatives."
    profession "Fishing" | "Secondary · Gathering" | "The quickest guide route is to keep Fishing close to your character level as you quest. These are suggested spots, not required fish counts. Wowhead: https://www.wowhead.com/classic/guide/fishing-leveling-1-300-wow-classic"
      step "1–75" | "Starting zones" | "Skill target 75" | "Fish inland Brilliant Smallfish or coastal Slitherskin Mackerel; a Shiny Bauble helps at low skill. Avoid Tirisfal on this route."
      step "75–150" | "Major faction cities" | "Skill target 150" | "Safe city water yields early Cooking fish, including Smallfish, Longjaw Mud Snapper, and Bristle Whisker Catfish."
      step "150–225" | "Stranglethorn Vale or Dustwallow Marsh" | "Skill target 225" | "Choose a faction-appropriate safe coast or inland spot; fish also support Cooking and Alchemy."
      step "225–300" | "Steamwheedle Port, Tanaris" | "Skill target 300" | "Stay here through 300, or switch to Feralas / Winterspring around 275."
    profession "First Aid" | "Secondary · Crafting" | "A short bandage ladder gets you to 300. Buy the Expert book and Heavy Silk / Mageweave manuals; the Artisan quest requires character level 35. Wowhead: https://www.wowhead.com/classic/guide/first-aid-leveling-1-300-wow-classic"
      step "1–50" | "Linen Bandage then Heavy Linen Bandage" | "40 + 10 crafts" | "1 Linen Cloth each for Linen Bandage; 2 Linen Cloth each for Heavy Linen Bandage. 160–180 Linen Cloth total through 125."
      step "51–80" | "Heavy Linen Bandage" | "30 crafts" | "2 Linen Cloth per bandage. Train Journeyman between skill 50 and 75."
      step "81–125" | "Wool then Heavy Wool Bandages" | "35 + 10 crafts" | "1 Wool Cloth per Wool Bandage; 2 Wool Cloth per Heavy Wool Bandage. 100–120 Wool Cloth total through 125."
      step "126–150" | "Heavy Wool Bandage" | "25 crafts" | "2 Wool Cloth each. Buy and learn Expert First Aid—Under Wraps between skill 125 and 150."
      step "151–180" | "Silk Bandage" | "30 crafts" | "1 Silk Cloth each. The 125–225 bracket uses 140–160 Silk Cloth total."
      step "181–210" | "Heavy Silk Bandage" | "30 crafts" | "2 Silk Cloth each. Learn from Manual: Heavy Silk Bandage."
      step "211–240" | "Mageweave Bandage" | "15 + 15 crafts" | "1 Mageweave Cloth each; 80–100 Mageweave Cloth total through 300. Learn from the vendor manual."
      step "241–260" | "Heavy Mageweave Bandage" | "20 crafts" | "2 Mageweave Cloth each; train from a First Aid doctor."
      step "261–290" | "Runecloth Bandage" | "30 crafts" | "1 Runecloth each; 80–100 Runecloth total through 300. Train from a First Aid doctor."
      step "290–300" | "Heavy Runecloth Bandage" | "10 crafts" | "2 Runecloth each; train from a First Aid doctor."
  activity
    event "Train" | "Rank gates" | "Train Journeyman, Expert, and Artisan before the next bracket caps; character level requirements apply to higher ranks."
    event "Craft" | "Save materials" | "Keep every intermediate explicitly marked as saved; later rows assume you have those outputs."
    event "Gather" | "Skill-based routes" | "Herbalism, Mining, Skinning, and Fishing use skill targets and locations rather than fixed make counts."
    event "Source" | "Wowhead Classic" | "Full references: wowhead.com/classic/guides/professions. Recipe colors, trainer details, and recipe availability are in the linked profession guides."
  footer
    text: "Route sources: Wowhead Classic profession leveling guides · Patch 1.15.8 · Counts may need adjustment for yellow / green skillups, recipes, or your realm's supply."
